# Two delay-coupled Stuart-Landau oscillators, z_j' = (1+i om) z_j - |z_j|^2 z_j + kappa (z_k(t-tau) - z_j).
# The in-phase wave has torus (Neimark-Sacker) bifurcations as tau increases (kappa=1, om=1.5: tau=1.584, 2.329).
# Torus curve (two parameters): Par1=tau, Par2=kappa as given; run the branch (Start -> Periodic), Axes -> Two par around
# the region (e.g. tau 1.3..2.4, kappa 0.5..1.6), Grab the first TR (label 2), Run -> Two Param.
# The simulation stores exactly one period (T=7.955487) of the in-phase wave at tau=1, to start Run -> Start -> Periodic.
par tau=1,kappa=1,om=1.5
x1'=x1-om*y1-(x1^2+y1^2)*x1+kappa*(delay(x2,tau)-x1)
y1'=om*x1+y1-(x1^2+y1^2)*y1+kappa*(delay(y2,tau)-y1)
x2'=x2-om*y2-(x2^2+y2^2)*x2+kappa*(delay(x1,tau)-x2)
y2'=om*x2+y2-(x2^2+y2^2)*y2+kappa*(delay(y1,tau)-y2)
init x1=1,y1=0,x2=1,y2=0
@ total=600.000000,trans=592.044513,dt=0.01,delay=4,meth=rungekutta
@ xlo=0,xhi=600,ylo=-1.5,yhi=1.5,maxstor=100000
done
